{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a redox-neutral photocatalytic CO2 fixation strategy using a proton-coupled electron transfer (PCET) manifold. By utilizing an organic photoredox catalyst (4CzIPN or derivatives), dihydropyridines (DHPs) as radical precursors, and an organic base (TBD), the authors achieved the carboxylation of benzylic positions to form synthetically relevant carboxylic acids under mild conditions. The mechanism involves the formation of a H-bonding complex between the DHP and TBD, facilitating a concerted PCET step followed by a radical-polar crossover to a carbanion that intercepts CO2.",
